 Noble PJ, Pritchard DM, Kennedy S, Hart CA, Dimaline R, Dockray GJ. Helicobacter pylori induces plasminogen activator inhibitor 2 in gastric epithelial cells through nuclear factor-kappaB and RhoA: implications for invasion and apoptosis. <source>Cancer Res</source> <volume>64</volume>: <fpage>1695</fpage>&#x02013;1702, <year>2004</year>.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14996729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r38"><label>38</label><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Varro</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name>, Noble PJ, Wroblewski LE, Bishop L, Dockray GJ. Gastrin-cholecystokinin(B) receptor expression in AGS cells is associated with direct inhibition and indirect stimulation of cell proliferation via paracrine activation of the epidermal growth factor receptor. <source>Gut</source> <volume>50</volume>: <fpage>827</fpage>&#x02013;833, <year>2002</year>.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12010885</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r39"><label>39</label><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Wacheck</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name>, Cejka D, Sieghart W, Losert D, Strommer S, Crevenna R, Monia BP, Selzer E. Mcl-1 is a relevant molecular target for antisense oligonucleotide strategies in gastric cancer cells. <source>Cancer Biol Ther</source> <volume>5</volume>: <fpage>1348</fpage>&#x02013;1354, <year>2006</year>.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16969094</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig position="float" id="f1"><label>Fig. 1.</label><caption><p>Western blots demonstrating time course of mcl-1, bcl-2, and bcl-x<sub>L</sub> expression in AGS-G<sub>R</sub> cells following treatment with 10 nM gastrin-17 (<italic>A</italic>), effects of various doses of gastrin-17 for 6 h on mcl-1 expression in AGS-G<sub>R</sub> cells (each concentration was assessed in 2 separate experiments) (<italic>B</italic>), and mcl-1 expression in AGS-G<sub>R</sub> and untransfected AGS cells 6 h after 10 nM gastrin (<italic>C</italic>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="zh30100852080001"></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="f2"><label>Fig. 2.</label><caption><p>Representative Western blot (<italic>A</italic>) and densitometric analysis (<italic>B</italic>) of individual Western blots from 3 separate experiments showing effects of treatment with 2 &#x003bc;g/ml actinomycin D (Act D) and 10 &#x003bc;g/ml cycloheximide (CHX) on mcl-1 expression in AGS-G<sub>R</sub> cells following treatment for 6 h with 10 nM gastrin-17. &#x0002a;<italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05 compared with gastrin treatment alone.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="zh30100852080002"></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="f3"><label>Fig. 3.</label><caption><p><italic>A</italic> and <italic>B</italic>: representative Western blots. <italic>C</italic>: densitometric analysis of individual Western blots from 3&#x02013;6 separate experiments showing effects of treatment with the CCK-2 receptor antagonist YM022 (10 nM), the protein kinase C (PKC) inhibitor Ro-32-0432 (1 &#x003bc;M), the MAP kinase (MAPK) inhibitor PD-98059 (20 &#x003bc;M), and the PI 3-kinase (PI3K) inhibitors LY-294002 (20 &#x003bc;M) and wortmannin (500 nM) on mcl-1 expression in AGS-G<sub>R</sub> cells following treatment for 6 h with 10 nM gastrin-17. &#x0002a;<italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05, &#x0002a;&#x0002a;<italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.01 compared with gastrin treatment alone.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="zh30100852080003"></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="f4"><label>Fig. 4.</label><caption><p>Representative Western blot (<italic>A</italic>) and densitometric analysis (<italic>B</italic>) of individual Western blots from 3 separate experiments showing effects of 24 h transfection with mcl-1 or control small-interfering RNA (siRNA) on mcl-1 protein expression in AGS-G<sub>R</sub> cells following treatment for 6 h with 10 nM gastrin-17. &#x0002a;<italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05 compared with gastrin-treated control siRNA-transfected cells. <italic>C</italic>: percentage apoptosis of AGS-G<sub>R</sub> cells transfected for 24 h with either mcl-1 or control siRNA, then treated for 6 h with serum-free medium in the absence or presence of 10 nM gastrin-17. &#x0002a;<italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05 between gastrin-treated and non-gastrin-treated cells following siRNA transfection.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="zh30100852080004"></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="f5"><label>Fig. 5.</label><caption><p>Immunohistochemical analysis of mcl-1 (<italic>A</italic>, <italic>C</italic>, <italic>E</italic>, <italic>G</italic>) and chromogranin A (<italic>B</italic>, <italic>D</italic>, <italic>F</italic>, <italic>H</italic>) expression in gastric biopsies from human patients with no pathology (<italic>A</italic> and <italic>B</italic>) or autoimmune atrophic gastritis, hypergastrinemia, and either nodular ECL cell hyperplasia (<italic>E</italic>, <italic>F</italic>, <italic>G</italic>, <italic>H</italic>) or frank gastric carcinoid tumors (<italic>C</italic>, <italic>D</italic>). Low-power (&#x000d7;10 objective) (<italic>A</italic>, <italic>B</italic>, <italic>E</italic>, <italic>F</italic>) and high-power (&#x000d7;40 objective) (<italic>C</italic>, <italic>D</italic>, <italic>G</italic>, <italic>H</italic>). Boxes shown in <italic>E</italic> and <italic>F</italic> are shown at higher magnification in <italic>G</italic> and <italic>H</italic>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="zh30100852080005"></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="f6"><label>Fig. 6.</label><caption><p>Immunohistochemical analysis of chromogranin A (<italic>A</italic>, <italic>E</italic>, <italic>H</italic>), cleaved caspase 3 (<italic>B</italic>, <italic>F</italic>), bcl-2 (<italic>C</italic>, <italic>G</italic>), and mcl-1 (<italic>D</italic>) expression in serial sections of gastric biopsies from a human patient with hypergastrinemia and nodular ECL cell hyperplasia. Low-power (&#x000d7;10 objective) (<italic>A</italic>, <italic>B</italic>, <italic>C</italic>, <italic>D</italic>) and high-power (&#x000d7;40 objective) (<italic>E</italic>, <italic>F</italic>, <italic>G</italic>, <italic>H</italic>). Boxes shown in <italic>A</italic>, <italic>B</italic>, and <italic>C</italic> are shown at higher magnification in <italic>E</italic> and <italic>H</italic>, <italic>F</italic>, and <italic>G</italic>, respectively. Arrows in <italic>F</italic> represent cleaved caspase 3-positive cells.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="zh30100852080006"></graphic></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="t1"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p>Results of mcl-1 immunohistochemistry in 10 patients with type 1 gastric carcinoid tumors secondary to atrophic gastritis and hypergastrinemia</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Patient Number</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Sex</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Age</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Anti GPC antibody</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Vitamin B12 Replacement</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom"><italic>H. pylori</italic> Serology</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom"><italic>H. pylori</italic> Present on Histology</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Fasting Serum Gastrin, pM</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Number of Nodules</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Maximum Nodule Size, mm</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Atrophic Gastritis</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Carcinoid Histology Confirmed</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Carcinoid mcl-1 Expression</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Nodular Hyperplasia Histology</t